**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

@issue-282 @bug @verify @deliver
Feature: Publish verification reports before delivery
  As a developer running nmg-sdlc execute
  I want passed verification evidence published before delivery
  So that the clean-tree delivery gate receives the exact verified head

  Scenario: Changed passing report is published
    Given verification produced a valid passing report
    And the report is the only non-runtime dirty path
    When verification finalization runs
    Then it stages only the report
    And commits it conventionally
    And pushes without force
    And writes a passed verify handoff for the published head

  Scenario: Already published report resumes without an empty commit
    Given the passing report is identical to HEAD
    And the branch is synchronized with its upstream
    When verification finalization runs
    Then no commit is created
    And the passed verify handoff advances to delivery

  Scenario Outline: Unsafe finalization fails closed
    Given verification finalization encounters <condition>
    When it attempts to publish the report
    Then it writes a failed intervention handoff
    And it does not write a passed handoff
    And delivery does not start

    Examples:
      | condition                         |
      | an unrelated dirty product path  |
      | a missing report                  |
      | a symlink report                  |
      | a staging failure                 |
      | a commit failure                  |
      | no configured upstream            |
      | a push failure                    |
      | branch divergence                 |

  Scenario: Failed verification is never published as success
    Given the report status is not Pass or PR Evidence Pending
    When verification finalization runs
    Then it does not publish a success commit
    And the failed handoff preserves the verification reason

  Scenario: Execute observes the published boundary
    Given finalization wrote a passed verify handoff
    When execute advances the issue queue
    Then delivery sees a clean tree at the report commit
    And exact-head PR safety remains authoritative
